From: AlterEgOS <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libcody: build with a C++20 host compiler (char8_t)

Since C++20 a u8"..." literal is a char8_t string, not a char string, so
libcody fails to build when the host compiler defaults to gnu++20 (GCC 16):

  client.cc:326:28: error: no match for 'operator==' (operand types are
  'std::string' and 'const char8_t [5]')
  client.cc:329:42: error: invalid conversion from 'const char8_t*' to 'size_t'

This is the libcody fix from GCC master (libcody/*.cc, cody.hh: cast the
literals, overloads taking char8_t where a literal is passed), backported
unchanged to GCC 13.3.0. Applied by Buildroot through BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR
to host-gcc-initial and host-gcc-final.

diff -ru a/libcody/buffer.cc b/libcody/buffer.cc
--- a/libcody/buffer.cc	2026-10-28 07:23:07.481809606 +0000
+++ b/libcody/buffer.cc	2026-10-28 07:23:07.895393807 +0000
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 namespace Cody {
 namespace Detail {
 
-static const char CONTINUE = S2C(u8";");
+static const unsigned char CONTINUE = S2C(u8";");
 
 void MessageBuffer::BeginLine ()
 {
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@
 
   for (std::string *word = nullptr;;)
     {
-      char c = *iter;
+      unsigned char c = *iter;
 
       ++iter;
       if (c == S2C(u8" ") || c == S2C(u8"\t"))
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@
 		  return EINVAL;
 		}
 
-	      if (c < S2C(u8" ") || c >= 0x7f)
+	      if (c < S2C(u8" "))
 		goto malformed;
 
 	      ++iter;
